iterations.reply:
I didn't add the `http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. This node's declared capabilities are only `response-channel`, and the graph definition hasn't been updated to grant more. The enrichment call would also send each customer's message text to an external host, which the node's confinement is meant to prevent. The blocks below implement the node as specified. Once the graph definition grants `http-client` and the enrichment requirement is documented there, it can be added in a separate change.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // requires: len(text) <= 100000 holds of every input, so no check is needed here.
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // ensures: delivered == true and present(session_id).
        // An output that violates the ensures cannot be returned, so trap instead.
        // panic = "abort" makes this a trap at the boundary.
        if !confirmation.delivered {
            panic!("SendReply: response channel did not confirm delivery");
        }
        if confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("SendReply: response channel returned no session identity");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

